    "bookid": 44,
    "chapterId": 215,
    "fileId": 18178,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Osteosarcoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<em>TP53</em> genetic alterations identified by whole-genome sequencing analysis of 20&nbsp;paediatric osteosarcomas are mapped onto schematic representations of the primary structure of p53, colour-coded by domain&nbsp;(<strong>a</strong>); the <em>TP53</em> gene structure (exons encoding distinct p53 domains are differentiated by a colour code)&nbsp;(<strong>b</strong>); and <em>TP53</em> exons&nbsp;1 and 2 and intron&nbsp;1&nbsp;(<strong>c</strong>). <em>TP53</em> structural variants (SVs) or mutations were found in 19&nbsp;tumours, and an <em>MDM2</em> amplification was found in 1&nbsp;tumour. A majority of the identified <em>TP53</em> SVs involved intron&nbsp;1.",
    "source": "The schematic image was modified from Chen et al. Cell Reports 7, 104-112. Is permission required from the journal?",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/44/215/18178.jpg",
